A||||11||mrfixit58||Bypassing the EGR||||5
Z||000000||mrfixit58||10-07-1999||05:32 PM||||Is there any real trick to bypassing the EGR valve? Which lines need to be plugged?<P>I've heard mixed opinions about the long term effects of bypassing the EGR. The opinions range from: "had mine off for two years with no effect"; to "if you remove the EGR the motor will run too lean and burn a piston". Anyone have any insite or real experience?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||88 Fiero||10-07-1999||06:17 PM||||Had mine off for longer than 2 years and no problem.. I have a V6..when you disengage the EGR you have to by pass the EGR Solenoid to fool the computer thinking it's still functional or else you will get a code in the ECM.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||10-07-1999||07:09 PM||||I've seen a lot of Fieros with the EGR removed... But what really is the advantage of removing it? Better mileage? More hp?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-07-1999||08:41 PM||||I believe that byassing the egr will give better part throttle response. As far as better mileage or HP, probably a little- but only in the throttle range that the egr operates in.||||reg||1
Z||000004||dans87gt||10-08-1999||07:51 AM||||I removed the EGR tube 6 years ago because I had two break and will not pay $100 for another, I didn't notice any HP gain or loss, but I did have to put black tape across the "check engine" light||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||10-08-1999||07:58 AM||||88 Fiero,<P>How do you bypass the EGR solinoid?||||reg||5
Z||000006||88 Fiero||10-08-1999||01:11 PM||||On the Solenoid for the EGR..there are 2 wires that you want to connect together and this fools the computer thinking that the EGR is functioning well. I will look into my car and let you know which wire and that way you can take the Solenoid out completely...||||reg||1
Z||000007||ka4nkf||10-08-1999||06:46 PM||||There Is Two Small Black Wires That Plug In Side By Side Into The Switch. Un-Plug These Wires And Connect Them Together. This Will Fool The Computer And Make It Think The Switch Is Made Up. No More Code 32.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ka4nkf||10-08-1999||06:58 PM||||I Forgot To Tell You Which Lines To Plug. Just Pull The One Off The EGR Valve And Plug It. Thats All.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfixit58||10-08-1999||07:50 PM||||ka4nkf,<P>Thanks for the assist. I'll give it a try.||||reg||14
Z||000010||terryk||10-09-1999||02:37 AM||||The 660 engines love to ping at high-part throttle with no EGR. When I switched ECM's and installed a knock sensor, the ping was obvious on the data stream. The engine noise made it hard to hear.||||reg||1
Z||000011||lowCG||10-09-1999||11:16 AM||||Can you help by using better gas,messing with the IAC,timing,putting resistors in the temp sensor circuit?<BR>Not that you want to cool the mixture with a rich condition,that would be counterproductive,but if you could keep in the range of the ox sensor,might work?<BR>What do you think Terry? <BR>||||reg||1
